            <ArticleTitle>Rectal examination in hospital patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rectal examination should be part of the initial examination of the patient especially those who are over the age of 50 and/or those with gastro intestinal and genito-urinary symptoms. We assessed the rate of rectal examinations carried out on acute general medical and surgical admissions over the age of 50 years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
